Roger performed his big hit, "Born Free" on this Gary Collins' Hour Magazine television show in 1986. Collins had starred in an NBC television adventure/drama series, "Born Free" in 1974, based on the movie by that name.  
Roger's "Born Free" reached #7 on the Billboard charts in 1966. Roger performed "Born Free" at the 1967 Academy Award Ceremony, that won 2 Oscars for Best Original Music Score and Best Song: https://youtu.be/XsjcBzaqis4.  Born Free, was a 1966 British documentary drama film of a real-life couple who raised Elsa the Lioness, an orphaned lion cub, to adulthood, and released her into the wilderness of Kenya. 
